<!--
    CLR host configuration for the MakeSfxCA-packaged managed custom action.

    MakeSfxCA wraps OllamaProxy.CustomActions.dll (net472, i.e. CLR 4.0) in a native SfxCA stub that
    Windows Installer loads. The stub picks the CLR version from THIS embedded config file. Without it,
    the stub falls back to the OLDEST installed runtime (CLR v2.0.50727) and then fails to load the 4.x
    assembly with a System.BadImageFormatException — which surfaces as custom-action error 1603 and rolls
    the whole install back (observed on WriteAppSettings during InstallFinalize).

    supportedRuntime pins CLR 4.0 (every .NET Framework 4.x shares the v4.0.30319 runtime). The legacy
    activation policy is the value DTF ships in its own sample and keeps mixed-mode activation working.

    This file is wired into the CA package as <Content> in OllamaProxy.CustomActions.csproj; the DTF
    targets forward project Content to MakeSfxCA, which embeds it next to the assembly as the .config.
-->
<configuration>
    <startup useLegacyV2RuntimeActivationPolicy="true">
        <supportedRuntime version="v4.0.30319" />
    </startup>
</configuration>
